From: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 16:33:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Documentation/networking: add flow_dissector consumer
 touch matrix

Add a new document describing struct flow_keys, the hash region
used by flow_hash_from_keys(), and which kernel subsystems read
which fields. Update the networking docs index to include it.

The consumer matrix is derived from an audit of nine kernel
flow_keys consumers (net/sched/{sch_cake,sch_choke,cls_flow},
net/ipv{4,6}/route, net/ipv{4,6}/netfilter, net/ipv4/fib_frontend,
net/core/flow_dissector). It documents the canonical 5-tuple
(addrs + ports + control.addr_type + basic.ip_proto) as the
highest-touch field set, identifies control.thoff as
direct-read-cold, and gives guidance for new consumers including
a pointer to flow_hash_from_keys_small() for 5-tuple-only
hashing.

This document provides the evidence base for two follow-up
patches that add flow_hash_from_keys_small() and adopt it in
sch_cake's host-accounting hashes.

No code change; pure documentation.

Signed-off-by: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
