+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+
+==================
+The flow dissector
+==================
+
+The flow dissector (``__skb_flow_dissect()`` and friends in
+``net/core/flow_dissector.c``) extracts protocol fields from a
+packet's network/transport headers and writes them into
+``struct flow_keys`` (declared in ``include/net/flow_dissector.h``).
+Many kernel subsystems consume the dissector's output for hash
+computation, flow classification, routing decisions, and
+filtering.
+
+This document describes ``struct flow_keys``, the hash region used
+by ``flow_hash_from_keys()``, and which subsystems read which
+fields. It is intended for developers adding new flow_keys
+consumers or considering layout changes.
+
+``struct flow_keys``
+====================
+
+The dissector's output struct holds a normalised view of a
+packet's headers::
+
+    struct flow_keys {
+        struct flow_dissector_key_control control;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_basic   basic;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_tags    tags;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_vlan    vlan;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_vlan    cvlan;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_keyid   keyid;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_ports   ports;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_icmp    icmp;
+        struct flow_dissector_key_addrs   addrs;
+        /* addrs MUST be the last member */
+    };
+
+``addrs`` is intentionally placed last because
+``flow_keys_hash_length()`` computes a variable hash length per
+``control.addr_type`` by subtracting the unused suffix of
+``addrs`` (IPv4 uses 8 of 32 bytes; IPv6 uses 32; TIPC uses 4).
+
+The hash region
+===============
+
+``flow_hash_from_keys()`` computes a SipHash2-4 over the
+``flow_keys`` bytes starting at the ``FLOW_KEYS_HASH_START_FIELD``
+macro (``basic``) and ending at the end of ``addrs``. The
+``control`` substruct sits before the hash region; its
+``addr_type`` field dispatches the consistentify pass that
+sorts source/destination pairs for bidirectional hash
+consistency.
+
+The hash region spans:
+
+- ``basic`` (n_proto, ip_proto)
+- ``tags`` (flow_label)
+- ``vlan`` (outer)
+- ``cvlan`` (inner)
+- ``keyid``
+- ``ports``
+- ``icmp``
+- ``addrs`` (variable: 8 B for IPv4, 32 B for IPv6, 4 B for TIPC)
+
+Hash length is 40 B for IPv4, 64 B for IPv6 (approximate; exact
+length depends on struct padding).
+
+Consumer touch patterns
+=======================
+
+The following subsystems are the principal consumers of
+``flow_keys`` data (i.e. they call ``skb_flow_dissect_flow_keys()``
+or read fields from a struct populated by it):
+
+================================ ===================================== ========================================================
+Consumer                         Bucket                                Fields read directly
+================================ ===================================== ========================================================
+``net/sched/sch_cake.c``         RX-hot (per-packet on busy queues)   ``control.addr_type``, ``ports``, ``addrs``
+``net/sched/sch_choke.c``        RX-hot                                (full hash via ``make_flow_keys_digest()``)
+``net/sched/cls_flow.c``         TC-hot (per matched filter)          ``control.addr_type``, ``basic.ip_proto``, ``ports``, ``addrs``
+``net/ipv4/route.c``             Route-hot (per routed packet)        ``control.{addr_type,flags}``, ``basic.ip_proto``, ``ports``, ``tags.flow_label``, ``addrs``
+``net/ipv6/route.c``             Route-hot                            ``control.{addr_type,flags}``, ``basic.ip_proto``, ``ports``, ``tags.flow_label``, ``addrs``
+``net/ipv4/fib_frontend.c``      Setup-only (RPF / source validate)  ``basic.ip_proto``, ``ports``
+``net/ipv4/netfilter.c``         Setup-only (ip_route_me_harder)      ``basic.ip_proto``, ``ports``
+``net/ipv6/netfilter.c``         Setup-only (ip6_route_me_harder)     ``basic.ip_proto``, ``ports``
+================================ ===================================== ========================================================
+
+Buckets describe where the consumer sits on the receive path:
+
+- **RX-hot**: per-packet on the ingress path (qdiscs on busy
+  queues).
+- **Route-hot**: per-packet that traverses the FIB lookup path.
+- **TC-hot**: per-packet, only when a TC filter chain matches.
+- **Setup-only**: per-flow or per-connection, not per-packet
+  (e.g. reverse-path-filter on RPF-enabled paths,
+  netfilter hook reroute).
+
+The Setup-only consumers (``fib_frontend``, ``netfilter``) read
+``flow_keys`` only via inline helpers
+(``fib4_rules_early_flow_dissect()`` / ``fib6_rules_early_flow_dissect()``
+in ``include/net/ip_fib.h`` and ``ip6_fib.h``). They consume
+``basic.ip_proto`` and ``ports`` directly, but read addresses from
+the IP header on the skb, not from the flow_keys ``addrs``
+field.
+
+Aggregate read frequency
+========================
+
+Reading the matrix column-wise, the fields touched by the most
+consumers are:
+
+- ``addrs`` — RX-hot + TC-hot + Route-hot×2
+- ``ports`` — RX-hot + TC-hot + Route-hot×2 + Setup-only×3
+- ``control.addr_type`` — RX-hot + TC-hot + Route-hot×2
+- ``basic.ip_proto`` — TC-hot + Route-hot×2 + Setup-only×3
+
+These four constitute the canonical 5-tuple plus the
+address-family dispatch field. They are the highest-touch
+fields and are written by the dissector on every IP packet.
+
+Fields touched only via the hash region (i.e. not directly read
+by any consumer's logic, but contributing to
+``flow_hash_from_keys()`` output):
+
+- ``basic.n_proto``, ``tags.flow_label`` (RX-hot consumers via hash),
+  ``vlan``, ``cvlan``, ``keyid``, ``icmp``
+
+``control.thoff`` is read by none of the surveyed consumers.
+
+Notes for new consumers
+=======================
+
+- If your consumer only needs the 5-tuple for a flow-identification
+  hash, prefer ``flow_hash_from_keys_small()`` over
+  ``flow_hash_from_keys()``. It hashes only ``basic.ip_proto +
+  ports + addrs`` and is roughly 50% faster for IPv4 with
+  statistically equivalent distribution for RSS-style indirection.
+  Note: it is **not** bit-exact with ``flow_hash_from_keys()`` and
+  is not suitable for comparing against ``skb->hash`` or for
+  hashes that need to align with the kernel's RSS path.
+- If your consumer reads only ``basic`` and ``ports`` (e.g.
+  Setup-only style usage), use the inline helpers in
+  ``include/net/ip_fib.h`` / ``ip6_fib.h`` to avoid full struct
+  setup.
+- Adding a new field to ``flow_keys`` is an ABI-affecting change.
+  The struct is used as the output of the BPF flow_dissector
+  hook; layout changes must preserve the byte offsets the
+  hook contract exposes.
+
+See also
+========
+
+- ``include/net/flow_dissector.h`` — struct definitions
+- ``net/core/flow_dissector.c`` — dissector implementation
+- ``Documentation/networking/scaling.rst`` — RSS / RPS / RFS
